WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:03.875
Shake a rope… and a wave runs along it.

00:04.867 --> 00:06.760
Keep your eye on the red dot.

00:07.287 --> 00:09.491
It only moves up and down!

00:09.597 --> 00:13.707
The wave carries energy along the rope not the rope itself.

00:13.884 --> 00:17.345
Shake faster, and the waves bunch closer together.

00:17.400 --> 00:19.962
But they DON'T travel any faster.

00:20.570 --> 00:22.810
Shake harder, and they grow taller…

00:22.830 --> 00:24.540
still at the same speed.

00:25.570 --> 00:29.389
The speed is set by the rope: v equals root T over

00:29.409 --> 00:30.199
mu.

00:30.730 --> 00:34.808
Now, send two equal and opposite pulses toward each other.

00:35.017 --> 00:38.124
For an instant… the rope goes flat.

00:39.068 --> 00:41.968
Then BOTH pulses come back, unchanged!

00:41.988 --> 00:44.429
Waves pass right through each other.

00:46.619 --> 00:51.479
LearnLoop AI. Predict. Watch. Explain.
